{
  "abstract": "A partial answer to problem 20.52 of the Kourovka Notebook (D. MacHale). For a finite group G of odd order, |G| - k(G) is a multiple of 16, where k(G) is the number of conjugacy classes (Burnside). The problem asks whether every multiple 16m, m > 0, is attained by a non-abelian group of odd order. This formalization proves that it is attained for every odd m and for every m in which 2 occurs to an odd power (m = 2, 6, 8, 10, 14, 18, ...). The groups are (Z/n : Z/3) x Z/a, with Z/3 acting on Z/n by an element u with u^2 + u + 1 = 0, taken with n = 7 and with n = 12 y^2 + 1 for y a power of two. Nothing is proved for m in which 2 occurs to an even power at least 2 (m = 4, 12, 16, 20, ...), so the problem itself stays open.",
